# PROVISION 1 — DEFINITIONS

For purposes of this License:

**“OneDraft™”** means the software project, platform, architecture, source code, domain model, APIs, documentation, implementation, interfaces, graphical systems, AI systems, project infrastructure, associated materials, and designated intellectual property comprising or supporting the OneDraft™ project.

**“Project”** means the OneDraft™ software project and its authorized development ecosystem.

**“Licensed Materials”** means source code, object code, schemas, specifications, documentation, examples, configuration, scripts, assets, interfaces, and other materials made available under this License.

**“Protected OneDraft Materials”** means materials owned or controlled by the OneDraft™ rights holder and included within the Project, including applicable source code, architecture, documentation, project-specific implementations, original designs, and associated intellectual property.

**“OneDraft Core”** means the foundational implementation and canonical domain architecture comprising the designated OneDraft™ project implementation.

**“Contributor”** means a person or organization submitting, authoring, modifying, or otherwise contributing material to the Project.

**“Authorized OneDraft Implementation”** means an implementation, modification, extension, deployment, or derivative work intended to develop, operate, maintain, test, improve, or otherwise advance OneDraft™ as the OneDraft™ project.

**“Independent Product”** means a software product, platform, service, framework, application, or other offering that is represented as separate from the OneDraft™ project.

**“Commercial Use”** means use for the purpose of generating revenue, providing paid services, licensing software, selling products, operating a commercial platform, or otherwise obtaining commercial benefit.

**“OneDraft Marks”** means OneDraft™, OneDraft, associated logos, product names, service names, visual identity, and other designated trademarks or project identifiers.

**“User Project Data”** means project information independently supplied, created, or controlled by a user through an authorized OneDraft implementation.

