* remove OneDraft™ project attribution for the purpose of concealing provenance;
* represent OneDraft™ source code as independently developed;
* create a substantially derived competing platform from the Licensed Materials and present it as unrelated to OneDraft™;
* or use the Licensed Materials to establish a separate project whose principal implementation is derived from OneDraft™ while intentionally obscuring that derivation.

This restriction does not prevent independent software development that does not copy or incorporate protected OneDraft™ materials.

